{ Dropping the reference requirement must not make the commands accept anything.

  <search> and <sort> are declared as <int[]> / <number[]>, so an argument that is no array at
  all is caught by the builtin signature instead - later than before, but with the type it was
  given rather than with the shape the parse tree happened to have. }

// EXPECT_ERROR Function <search> expects int\[\] as argument type

on init
    declare a := 3
    message(search(a + 1, 3))
end on
